# One A-B dimer held together by its y sites, with free x sites that can
# join only inside the complex (issue #139).  The `+` says the rule binds
# two complexes and unbinds into two, so BNG2's network has no reaction
# that closes the x ring: its reactions join dimers into chains, and with
# one dimer none of them can fire.  With
# block_same_complex_binding off (the deprecated -no-bscb), RM tests
# neither half of the `+`: the ring closes at kf and opens at kr, as in
# NFsim run with neither -cb nor -bscb.
begin model
begin parameters
  kf 1
  kr 1
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(x,y)
  B(x,y)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(x,y!1).B(x,y!1) 1
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Closed A(x!+)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  Ring: A(x) + B(x) <-> A(x!1).B(x!1) kf, kr
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
